  "description": "#6758 — a `datetime` definition and its values. `create_property_def` takes `datetime` (migration 0134); under it `set_property` takes `value_date` in the stored form only, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MMZ` in UTC naming a real date and time (`validate_property_value`), and refuses a local time, a time with an offset, seconds and a day with `validation`; the stored form is a date under no other key. Reading a user's text into the stored form (`read_datetime`) is the caller's, so no step depends on the host's time zone but the day filters (the Pages view, the References panel, `filtered_blocks_query`, `query_by_property`, #6906): a day operand reads a stored instant as the device's day, and each value at noon UTC is on its UTC day from UTC-11 to UTC+11. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
